=== PARITY (vs web EventTimeline.tsx) ===
  Data sources -> bound via the shared state-holder seam (EventTimelineSource ->
    EventTimelineModel): useTranslation (the P1/S10 facade) + useTimelineLabels (ported to
    the pure EventTimelineLabels resolver). The web leaf receives an already-derived
    `timelineEvents` prop from its parent (the Security & Access page's deriveTimeline(history));
    the native source carries the cached security history + load/freshness state and the model
    reproduces deriveTimeline, so the derivation is exercised end-to-end (the 0009 pattern). The
    view performs NO HTTP.
  Projection -> EventTimelineAdapter.deriveTimeline is a 1:1 port of helpers.deriveTimeline:
    sort newest-first; diff each record vs the next-older one; emit a lock row on a `locked`
    change (variant locked?positive:negative, detail = doorState string ?? "—"), a sentry row on
    a `sentryMode` change (variant isSentryActive?positive:negative), a door row on a `doorState`
    change (variant doorClosed?positive:negative, detail = doorState string ?? closed?"Closed":
    "Open"); cap at 50; return newest-first. isSentryActive (!contains "off") + doorClosed
    (absent/"closed"/"0"/"false") ported verbatim. ALL verified by EXECUTED XCTest.
  Composition -> web `FadeIn delay={0.35}` + `GlassPanel p-4` reproduced with TSFadeIn(0.35) +
    tsGlassPanel; the h2 title (text-lg) -> Font.TS.section header; each row is the web
    `flex items-start gap-3 rounded-lg bg-white/[0.02] p-3`: a variant-tinted icon circle
    (positive->green, negative->red, neutral->gray) with the timelineIcon SF Symbol
    (lock.fill/lock.open.fill, checkmark.shield.fill/exclamationmark.shield.fill,
    door.left.hand.closed/door.left.hand.open) + title/subtitle + absolute timestamp; the list
    scrolls within the web max-h-96 (384pt) cap.
  Shared components -> @/components/ui/GlassPanel -> tsGlassPanel (TSMaterial);
    @/components/data-display TimeStamp -> EventTimelineTimestamp.absolute; @/components/feedback/
    EmptyState -> TSEmptyState; @/components/motion/FadeIn -> TSFadeIn. Compiled against the REAL
    apps/apple library (tokens + Badges/TSTone + Material + Motion) in the iOS 18 + macOS 15
    typechecks below. Recharts -> none / Leaflet -> none (no chart/map on this surface).
  States (all render) -> content (scrollable timeline list) · empty (web EmptyState "No state
    changes detected in the history.") · loading (skeleton rows) · error (QueryError-equivalent
    retry — native chrome, since the web leaf relies on its parent's react-query) · stale (chip +
    banner + one guarded auto-refresh) · offline (cached rows + chip + banner). Cached rows stay
    visible behind refresh/failure. Each has a #if DEBUG preview + is unit-tested via the
    projection.
  i18n -> all 12 source keys resolve through the P1/S10 facade (table "EventTimeline") with the
